{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Forward node2 inventory application logs to node1 and persist them at /var/log/inventory/node2.log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The forwarding and collector configurations validated successfully. An inventory-tagged record generated on node2 appeared exactly once at the required node1 path, while unrelated control records were excluded. Final evidence showed four inventory records, secure file metadata, an active collector, and a live sender connection.","evidence_ids":["cmd-732d57da31b94115","cmd-131d2f8b687441ae","cmd-b0470d7be40f4575","cmd-9be5131bdfbc4c7e","cmd-072eff176a5a4ce5"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep logging functional through and after a restart of node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Evidence shows a healthy pre-restart collector, acknowledged restart, observed collector unavailability, a changed boot identity, restored listener and service, preserved earlier data, and exact-once delivery of a record generated during the outage.","evidence_ids":["cmd-92060aad5d6a48eb","cmd-50a6442e4d8a4739","cmd-108f1581c78b4e87","cmd-16e450cf45b24155","cmd-cb197d115ea24859","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep logging functional after a restart of node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 had a healthy service and connection before the acknowledged restart; its temporary unavailability was observed, its boot identity changed, rsyslog and SSH recovered automatically, and a new post-restart inventory record reached node1 exactly once.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8bc8fc5a4ff14bec","cmd-90c1fe4f76784a95","cmd-bb1705330f314abd","cmd-9be5131bdfbc4c7e","cmd-072eff176a5a4ce5","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use platform-compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0. The executor used the preinstalled RHEL rsyslog package, configurations validated and ran successfully, and final package-health checks remained clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-81dc265b028b4cad","cmd-2d3f317061ec430d","cmd-9be5131bdfbc4c7e","cmd-072eff176a5a4ce5","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.99,"summary":"Operational hygiene was excellent: final services and package state were healthy, exposure was restricted, temporary validation output was removed, and no failed units remained. The only unnecessary mutation was creation of an empty rollback directory on node2; it contributed no backup or task state and was later fully removed. The retained node1 firewall backup had a clear rollback purpose and was protected.","evidence_ids":["cmd-732d57da31b94115","cmd-9be5131bdfbc4c7e","cmd-072eff176a5a4ce5","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Direct behavior tests establish forwarding to the required file, recovery across separate restarts of both nodes, queued delivery during the collector outage, and preservation of the operating-system release and kernel. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and corroborated by the fixed boot-identity snapshots.","limitations":["Discovery found no running inventory application, so routing was tested with synthetic logger records using the inventory program tag. This directly verifies the logging path but not a separate application's emission behavior (cmd-f9eeabc414d54138, cmd-131d2f8b687441ae)."]}
